### Describe the bug

Svelte 5.11 generates unique animation name even if `animation:` rule is inside `:global {}`.

Input:

```svelte
<progress class="loader"></progress>

<style>
  :global {
    .loader:indeterminate::-moz-progress-bar {
      animation: --loader-bouncing 1.8s infinite;
    }
    @keyframes --loader-bouncing {
      100% {
        width: 25%;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
```

Expected (Svelte 5.10):

```css
  /* :global {*/
    .loader:indeterminate::-moz-progress-bar {
      animation: --loader-bouncing 1.8s infinite;
    }
    @keyframes --loader-bouncing {
      100% {
        width: 25%;
      }
    }
  /*}*/
```

Actual (5.10.1…5.13):

```css

  /* :global {*/
    .loader:indeterminate::-moz-progress-bar {
      animation: svelte-17rbc26---loader-bouncing 1.8s infinite;
    }
    @keyframes --loader-bouncing {
      100% {
        width: 25%;
      }
    }
  /*}*/
```

We have the same issue in Svelte 5.13 too.

### Reproduction

Latest 5.13.0 broken output:
https://svelte.dev/playground/3a7853b61a544714be1740178439fefa?version=5.13.0

Svelte 5.11.0 broken output:
https://svelte.dev/playground/3a7853b61a544714be1740178439fefa?version=5.11.0

Svelte 5.10.0 fixed output:
https://svelte.dev/playground/3a7853b61a544714be1740178439fefa?version=5.10.0

